#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083065 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083272 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "332fefd8-7de7-5a84-81e2-a2aa97be9b73" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value for a Random Variable with Uniform Probability"}] :question/id #uuid "27a80de6-49d0-557b-8444-ebab046e795b" :question/math-academy-id "e-6074" :question/problem "What is the expected value of one roll of a tetrahedral die?" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\sum\\limits_{x \\in S} x \\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nA tetrahedral die has four sides. Let $X$ be the score attained on a random roll of the die. Then the support is $S = \\{ 1,2,3,4 \\},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\dfrac{1}{4}{:}$\n\n$$\nf(1) = f(2) = f(3) = f(4) = \\dfrac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{4})+2(\\frac{1}{4})+3(\\frac{1}{4})+4(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{2}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{4}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+2+3+4}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{4} \\\\  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083066 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90d0c882-c94b-5759-9a78-63979365e318" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Profit of a Game"}] :question/id #uuid "2b946455-893f-57db-b0a5-d52091914cf2" :question/math-academy-id "e-6075" :question/problem "Suppose that we play a game with a stack of five cards labeled $1$ through $5.$ A card is drawn at random. Drawing $1,2,3,$ or $4$ means that you lose $\\[math]1,$ and drawing a $5$ means that you win $\\[/math] 5.$ What is the expected profit at each drawing in this game?" :question/worked-solution "Let $p$ represent the profit on a draw in this game. On each draw in the game, there are two possible outcomes:\n\n- drawing $1,2,3,4$, the player loses $\\[math]1,$ so we have $p=-1.$\n\n- drawing $5$, the player wins $\\[/math]5,$ so we have $p=5.$\n\nThe probabilities for the outcomes are\n\n$$\nP(-1)=\\dfrac{4}{5}, \\qquad P(5)=\\dfrac{1}{5}.\n$$\n\nLet's summarize this in a table.  If $p$ is the profit (in dollars) on a single draw, and $f(p)$ is the probability mass function for $p,$ then we have the following:\n\n| $p$ | $-1$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(p)$ | $\\dfrac{4}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ |\n\nTherefore, the expected value of $p$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\textrm E[p] &= -1 \\cdot f(-1) + 5 \\cdot f(5)  \\[5pt]\n&= -1 \\left( \\dfrac{4}{5} \\right) + 5 \\left( \\dfrac{1}{5} \\right)  \\[5pt]\n\t&=-\\dfrac{4}{5} + 1 \\[3pt]\n\t&=\\dfrac{1}{5} \\[3pt]\n\t&=0.2\n\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected profit at each draw in this game is $\\[math]0.20$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083108 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083308 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8297713-fb86-59f2-af4d-850af2575541" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value for a Random Variable with Non-Uniform Probability"}] :question/id #uuid "e6dd60de-5df1-531d-9971-847343303fd7" :question/math-academy-id "e-7383" :question/problem "The rolls of an unfair tetrahedral die follow the probability mass function $f(x)$ as shown in the table below. What is the expected value of one roll of the die?\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\dfrac{1}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ |" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\sum\\limits_{x \\in S} x \\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{10})+2(\\frac{3}{10})+3(\\frac{2}{5})+4(\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}+\\frac{6}{10}+\\frac{6}{5}+\\frac{4}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}+\\frac{6}{10}+\\frac{12}{10}+\\frac{8}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+6+12+8}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{10} \\\\  & =2.7\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083109 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083309 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c3fc090-22e5-5f05-9634-b8c645cf5700" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value Given the Frequency of a Random Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "ed80b546-956c-5b67-ac7d-0c0049c2278c" :question/math-academy-id "e-7385" :question/problem "Several children were asked about how many pets they have. The results were recorded below. If $X$ is the number of pets that a randomly selected child has, what is the expected value of $X?$\n\n| Number of pets | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Number of Children | $5$ | $6$ | $5$ |" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\sum\\limits_{x \\in S} x \\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nWe're given the frequencies of the number of pets, so we can start by computing the corresponding probabilities. The total number of children is $5+6+5=16,$ so the corresponding probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0)=f(0) & =\\frac{5}{16} \\\\ P(X=1)=f(1) & =\\frac{6}{16}=\\frac{3}{8} \\\\ P(X=2)=f(2) & =\\frac{5}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe organize these results in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\dfrac{5}{16}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{8}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{16}$ |\n\nNow, summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{5}{16})+1(\\frac{3}{8})+2(\\frac{5}{16}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{3}{8}+\\frac{10}{16} \\\\  & =0+\\frac{6}{16}+\\frac{10}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+6+10}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{16} \\\\  & =1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262744 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083308 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8297713-fb86-59f2-af4d-850af2575541" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value for a Random Variable with Non-Uniform Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e77bbba-6d78-5114-b600-9c7f71e65420" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{35}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260009} {:answer/id #uuid "447f8063-1baf-5c4a-9b97-4a25fc328415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260473} {:answer/id #uuid "4ec2e1ee-da93-5494-b50c-58b008ea1ff2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{35}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260545} {:answer/id #uuid "85075ebd-c155-585d-a463-64d1c425a07b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{29}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261030} {:answer/id #uuid "b0beacca-b6b9-5b56-9e34-2ad8f29a0929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ec2e1ee-da93-5494-b50c-58b008ea1ff2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{35}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260545} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd47829e-aabc-5fbe-b4ee-de0c0b559504" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262507}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e811f3df-a27f-5fdf-9386-dd1c84fc9cd9" :question/math-academy-id "q-127269" :question/problem "The absolute difference between the outcomes of one roll of two fair six-sided dice follows the probability mass function $f(x)$ shown in the table below. What is the expected value of the absolute difference of the outcomes for one roll of the two dice?\n\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{5}{18}$ | $\\frac{4}{18}$ | $\\frac{3}{18}$ | $\\frac{2}{18}$ | $\\frac{1}{18}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4)+5\\cdot f(5) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{6})+1(\\frac{5}{18})+2(\\frac{4}{18})+3(\\frac{3}{18})+4(\\frac{2}{18})+5(\\frac{1}{18}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{5}{18}+\\frac{8}{18}+\\frac{9}{18}+\\frac{8}{18}+\\frac{5}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+5+8+9+8+5}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370946 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083309 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c3fc090-22e5-5f05-9634-b8c645cf5700" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value Given the Frequency of a Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28ce0594-ae9a-5533-b4e8-9b16a4434e24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370948} {:answer/id #uuid "dc2d678f-d252-5400-be5e-828422888057" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{70}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370949} {:answer/id #uuid "39a17018-6a1b-5fa0-a4b2-d57693172562" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370950} {:answer/id #uuid "4b8d0e30-5870-5882-90fe-bbe6d3d8ae98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{110}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370951} {:answer/id #uuid "11bce5a2-21ae-5099-bf11-e90bee429d37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b8d0e30-5870-5882-90fe-bbe6d3d8ae98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{110}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370951} :answer-field/id #uuid "45d39d50-e814-58b3-b920-cbbb549d00fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370947}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3b33e7f8-97bd-52b2-9fc5-eb73c2b2d7ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-42732" :question/problem "A bag contains $4$ five-dollar bills, $8$ ten-dollar bills, and $6$ twenty-dollar bills. If one bill is randomly drawn from a bag, what is its expected value?" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the value of a randomly drawn bill. Then the support is $S={5,10,20}.$\n\nIn the bag there are  $4$ five-dollar bills, $8$ ten-dollar bills and $6$ twenty-dollar bills (eighteen bills in total), so the probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(5) & =\\frac{4}{18}=\\frac{2}{9} \\\\ P(10) & =\\frac{8}{18}=\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ P(20) & =\\frac{6}{18}=\\frac{3}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =5\\cdot f(5)+10\\cdot f(10)+20\\cdot f(20) \\\\  & =5(\\frac{2}{9})+10(\\frac{4}{9})+20(\\frac{3}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{9}+\\frac{40}{9}+\\frac{60}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{10+40+60}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{110}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354279 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083308 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8297713-fb86-59f2-af4d-850af2575541" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value for a Random Variable with Non-Uniform Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ab16145-6ff1-5809-bb97-adbc45c2e916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351662} {:answer/id #uuid "639ce162-6deb-5cdc-aa12-71b9f5fbe5eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352452} {:answer/id #uuid "bd54336d-b9c4-5711-b627-5b941c66a638" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353180} {:answer/id #uuid "d0020f69-096b-56d4-a5e8-6e4bfea46ab2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353367} {:answer/id #uuid "fe9d5f73-8fdc-5a4b-a70a-fdac1c36f988" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe9d5f73-8fdc-5a4b-a70a-fdac1c36f988" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353802} :answer-field/id #uuid "30e0cc8e-72a3-5b78-8684-26b6a6384b0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353899}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5e4d143c-c13b-5ae0-a77b-3da97ad8ff9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-84020" :question/problem "The number of heads facing upward after tossing $2$ unfair coins follows the probability mass function $f(x)$ shown in the table below. What is the expected value of the number of heads facing upward after tossing the $2$ coins?\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{4}{9}$ | $\\frac{4}{9}$ |" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{9})+1(\\frac{4}{9})+2(\\frac{4}{9}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{4}{9}+\\frac{8}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{4+8}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357384 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083272 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "332fefd8-7de7-5a84-81e2-a2aa97be9b73" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Expected Value for a Random Variable with Uniform Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2caf601c-b68b-5641-9bcb-7727613b6286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355049} {:answer/id #uuid "b09bb1f2-5bf8-596e-9a70-aa6dafe756fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356220} {:answer/id #uuid "c7862014-d396-52a6-aec9-f81ecf2bc212" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356408} {:answer/id #uuid "e0768a45-d865-522f-9029-613b3fa804b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356627} {:answer/id #uuid "f65fe058-9b55-5802-9726-5819e6757757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f65fe058-9b55-5802-9726-5819e6757757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356810} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d0c6279-c1f7-5afc-9b15-a7d1f211a92a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357041}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7272ef45-cd69-5899-b223-f4105223d0d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-89152" :question/problem "A fair spinner has six sides each labeled $-2,$ $-1,$ $1,$ $3,$ $5,$ and $6.$ If spinner is spun, what is its expected value?" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the spin of the fair spinner. Then the support is $S={-2,-1,1,3,5,6},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{6}:$\n\n$$\nf(-2)=f(-1)=f(1)=f(3)=f(5)=f(6)=\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =(-2)\\cdot f(-2)+(-1)\\cdot f(-1)+1\\cdot f(1)+3\\cdot f(3)+5\\cdot f(5)+6\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =(-2)(\\frac{1}{6})+(-1)(\\frac{1}{6})+1(\\frac{1}{6})+3(\\frac{1}{6})+5(\\frac{1}{6})+6(\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{6}+\\frac{-1}{6}+\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{3}{6}+\\frac{5}{6}+\\frac{6}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-1+1+3+5+6}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{6} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
